{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TVuXNKz1numYjrku7WuTud","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# PENILAIAN PRESTASI / PERFORMANCE ASSESSMENT\n2\t\n3\t**Kod WIM / WIM Code:** G452-010-3:2023-C01/PA\n4\t**Kertas Warna / Paper Color:** BIRU MUDA / LIGHT BLUE (Ocean Blue)\n5\t\n6\t---\n7\t\n8\t## Competency Unit: Perform BEV Scheduled Maintenance (G452-010-3:2023-C01)\n9\t\n10\t| Field | Detail |\n11\t|-------|--------|\n12\t| Duration | 2 hours 30 minutes |\n13\t| Total Marks | 100 |\n14\t| Passing Mark | 60% (60 marks) |\n15\t| Work Activities Covered | WA1, WA2, WA3 |\n16\t\n17\t---\n18\t\n19\t## Instructions to Candidates\n20\t\n21\t1. This performance assessment consists of THREE (3) practical tasks\n22\t2. Complete ALL tasks within the allocated time\n23\t3. Follow all safety procedures — failure to comply with critical safety requirements results in automatic failure\n24\t4. You will be assessed on PROCESS, OUTPUT, ATTITUDE, SAFETY, and ENVIRONMENT\n25\t5. A training BEV and fully equipped work bay will be provided\n26\t\n27\t---\n28\t\n29\t## TASK 1: BEV Scheduled Maintenance Workplace Preparation (25 marks)\n30\t**Time Allocation: 30 minutes**\n31\t**Reference: WA1 — KK(1/3)**\n32\t\n33\tPrepare a BEV maintenance work bay for a scheduled maintenance service. You must:\n34\t\n35\t1. Inspect and don all required PPE correctly (5 marks)\n36\t2. Set up the work bay with barrier stanchions and HV signage (4 marks)\n37\t3. Verify all safety equipment: fire extinguisher (Class D), electric rescue hook, safety box (4 marks)\n38\t4. Inspect insulated tools and common tools; remove any defective items (4 marks)\n39\t5. Complete a Job Hazard Analysis (JHA) form for BEV scheduled maintenance (5 marks)\n40\t6. Conduct a toolbox talk covering task overview, hazards, PPE, and emergency procedures (3 marks)\n41\t\n42\t---\n43\t\n44\t## TASK 2: BEV Health Check Activities (40 marks)\n45\t**Time Allocation: 60 minutes**\n46\t**Reference: WA2 — KK(2/3)**\n47\t\n48\tPerform a complete BEV health check on the provided training vehicle. You must:\n49\t\n50\t1. Verify vehicle information: registration, VIN, mileage (4 marks)\n51\t2. Perform a systematic exterior walk-around inspection (6 marks)\n52\t3. Perform an interior systems check (4 marks)\n53\t4. Connect the diagnostic scan tool and perform a full system scan (5 marks)\n54\t5. Read and record all fault codes with freeze frame data (5 marks)\n55\t6. Perform BEV-specific system checks: battery SOC/SOH, cell voltages, insulation resistance, thermal management, charging status (8 marks)\n56\t7. Perform component active tests as supported by the diagnostic tool (3 marks)\n57\t8. Prepare and submit a complete BEV health check report with condition ratings and recommendations (5 marks)\n58\t\n59\t---\n60\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e8b3354b-5830-4547-91a0-f5b7d5e503e0","uuid":"630840e9-b560-480c-b6fe-63a1aaf26a0b","timestamp":"2026-04-17T10:31:30.635Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\noss-to-wim\\bev-diagnostic-rectification\\C01\\PA.md","content":"# PENILAIAN PRESTASI / PERFORMANCE ASSESSMENT\n\n**Kod WIM / WIM Code:** G452-010-3:2023-C01/PA\n**Kertas Warna / Paper Color:** BIRU MUDA / LIGHT BLUE (Ocean Blue)\n\n---\n\n## Competency Unit: Perform BEV Scheduled Maintenance (G452-010-3:2023-C01)\n\n| Field | Detail |\n|-------|--------|\n| Duration | 2 hours 30 minutes |\n| Total Marks | 100 |\n| Passing Mark | 60% (60 marks) |\n| Work Activities Covered | WA1, WA2, WA3 |\n\n---\n\n## Instructions to Candidates\n\n1. This performance assessment consists of THREE (3) practical tasks\n2. Complete ALL tasks within the allocated time\n3. Follow all safety procedures — failure to comply with critical safety requirements results in automatic failure\n4. You will be assessed on PROCESS, OUTPUT, ATTITUDE, SAFETY, and ENVIRONMENT\n5. A training BEV and fully equipped work bay will be provided\n\n---\n\n## TASK 1: BEV Scheduled Maintenance Workplace Preparation (25 marks)\n**Time Allocation: 30 minutes**\n**Reference: WA1 — KK(1/3)**\n\nPrepare a BEV maintenance work bay for a scheduled maintenance service. You must:\n\n1. Inspect and don all required PPE correctly (5 marks)\n2. Set up the work bay with barrier stanchions and HV signage (4 marks)\n3. Verify all safety equipment: fire extinguisher (Class D), electric rescue hook, safety box (4 marks)\n4. Inspect insulated tools and common tools; remove any defective items (4 marks)\n5. Complete a Job Hazard Analysis (JHA) form for BEV scheduled maintenance (5 marks)\n6. Conduct a toolbox talk covering task overview, hazards, PPE, and emergency procedures (3 marks)\n\n---\n\n## TASK 2: BEV Health Check Activities (40 marks)\n**Time Allocation: 60 minutes**\n**Reference: WA2 — KK(2/3)**\n\nPerform a complete BEV health check on the provided training vehicle. You must:\n\n1. Verify vehicle information: registration, VIN, mileage (4 marks)\n2. Perform a systematic exterior walk-around inspection (6 marks)\n3. Perform an interior systems check (4 marks)\n4. Connect the diagnostic scan tool and perform a full system scan (5 marks)\n5. Read and record all fault codes with freeze frame data (5 marks)\n6. Perform BEV-specific system checks: battery SOC/SOH, cell voltages, insulation resistance, thermal management, charging status (8 marks)\n7. Perform component active tests as supported by the diagnostic tool (3 marks)\n8. Prepare and submit a complete BEV health check report with condition ratings and recommendations (5 marks)\n\n---\n","numLines":60,"startLine":1,"totalLines":149}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01CArAaLnKnGbjc1HVc4njMJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014p6E2aqsQ58ctbzVhbHR6R","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\noss-to-wim\\aesthetic-services\\C01\\PA.md","limit":60},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":965,"cache_read_input_tokens":36838,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":965},"output_tokens":58,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e8b3354b-5830-4547-91a0-f5b7d5e503e0","uuid":"c7d4b9f5-b8ac-4557-afd9-f0c0b6e2953d"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014p6E2aqsQ58ctbzVhbHR6R","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# PENILAIAN PRESTASI / PERFORMANCE ASSESSMENT\n2\t\n3\t**Kod / Code:** S960-002-3:2020-C01/PA\n4\t**Competency Unit:** C01 — Body Consultation / *Konsultasi Badan*\n5\t**Paper Colour / Warna Kertas:** LIGHT BLUE / BIRU MUDA\n6\t**Duration / Tempoh:** 60 Minutes / 60 Minit (3 × 20 min scenarios)\n7\t**Total Marks / Jumlah Markah:** 100\n8\t**Passing Mark / Markah Lulus:** 70/100 (minimum Score 3/5 on ALL rubric criteria)\n9\t\n10\t---\n11\t\n12\t## Arahan / Instructions\n13\t\n14\t1. You will assess THREE (3) client consultation scenarios in sequence.\n15\t2. Each scenario is 15–20 minutes and is assessed independently.\n16\t3. For each scenario, score the candidate on FOUR (4) rubric criteria using a 5-point scale.\n17\t4. A score of **3 or above** on each criterion is required to PASS that criterion.\n18\t5. Any criterion scored **2 or below** = NOT YET COMPETENT for that scenario.\n19\t6. Candidate must pass ALL criteria in at least 2 of 3 scenarios to be declared COMPETENT.\n20\t7. Record marks in the tables below. Provide written feedback where scoring ≤ 2.\n21\t\n22\t---\n23\t\n24\t## SENARIO 1 — Saringan Sejarah Kesihatan / Health History Screening\n25\t\n26\t**Client Profile:** Madam Rosnah, 42 years old, female office manager. Presents with persistent fatigue\n27\tand mild lower-back ache. She has hypertension (on medication) and a known shellfish allergy.\n28\tShe has never received body therapy services before.\n29\t\n30\t**Task:** Conduct a full body consultation from work area preparation through contraindication screening,\n31\tBMI calculation, and post-consultation advice. Duration: 15–20 minutes.\n32\t\n33\t**NOSS Reference:** WA 1 (1.1–1.3), WA 2 (2.1–2.3), WA 3 (3.1–3.2, 3.6–3.7, 3.9–3.11), WA 4 (4.1–4.4)\n34\t\n35\t### Rubrik Penilaian — Senario 1 / Assessment Rubric — Scenario 1\n36\t\n37\t| Kriteria / Criteria | 5 — Cemerlang | 4 — Memuaskan | 3 — Kompeten | 2 — Sedang Membangun | 1 — Tidak Kompeten | Markah |\n38\t|---------------------|---------------|----------------|--------------|----------------------|--------------------|--------|\n39\t| **S1-A Communication Effectiveness** (*Keberkesanan Komunikasi*) | Greets professionally; explains all steps clearly; uses empathetic, positive language; checks client understanding throughout; bilingual where appropriate | Greets and explains most steps; mostly clear communication; minor lapses in rapport | Adequate greeting and explanation; client understood key steps; basic professional conduct maintained | Communication partial; some steps not explained; client visibly confused at least once | No professional greeting; steps unexplained; client confused or uncomfortable throughout | /5 |\n40\t| **S1-B Health & Allergy Data Collection** (*Pengumpulan Data Kesihatan & Alahan*) | ALL fields in personal profile recorded; hypertension medication AND shellfish allergy both documented; PDPA consent obtained; contraindications checklist fully completed and verified | Hypertension and allergy recorded; PDPA obtained; 1–2 minor fields missed | Hypertension OR allergy recorded; PDPA obtained; consultation card mostly complete | One major contraindication missed (hypertension or allergy not recorded) | Both contraindications missed; PDPA not obtained | /5 |\n41\t| **S1-C Skin Condition Assessment Accuracy** (*Ketepatan Penilaian Kulit*) | Body type, posture (3 views), figure faults, skin/muscular/adipose/cellulite all assessed and correctly classified with explanation | All assessments done; classification correct; minimal explanation given | Most assessments done; at least 4 of 6 body analysis components completed | Assessments incomplete; fewer than 4 body analysis components; significant inaccuracies | No structured body analysis performed | /5 |\n42\t| **S1-D Recommendation Appropriateness** (*Kesesuaian Cadangan*) | Salon service plan avoids electrotherapy (contraindicated by hypertension); safe alternatives recommended; shellfish-derived products excluded; home care complete and appropriate | Service plan appropriate; safe alternatives offered; 1 minor oversight in exclusion | Electrotherapy contraindication acknowledged; safe treatment offered; home care provided | Service plan partially appropriate; one unsafe recommendation present | Contraindications ignored in service plan; potentially harmful treatment recommended | /5 |\n43\t\n44\t**Subtotal Scenario 1:** \\_\\_\\_\\_ / 20 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; **Pass (≥12/20, no criterion <3):** ☐ YES &nbsp; ☐ NO\n45\t\n46\t---\n47\t\n48\t## SENARIO 2 — Analisis Kulit & Komposisi Badan / Skin & Body Composition Analysis\n49\t\n50\t**Client Profile:** Ms. Adilah, 28 years old, female, post-pregnancy (8 months postpartum). She is\n51\tconcerned about stretch marks (*striae*) on her abdomen and thighs, loose skin, and excess adipose\n52\taround the waist. No known allergies. Currently breastfeeding.\n53\t\n54\t**Task:** Perform detailed skin condition analysis, body composition assessment, BMI calculation,\n55\tand design a safe service plan appropriate for postpartum and breastfeeding status.\n56\tDuration: 15–20 minutes.\n57\t\n58\t**NOSS Reference:** WA 3 (3.3–3.8), WA 4 (4.1–4.2)\n59\t\n60\t### Rubrik Penilaian — Senario 2 / Assessment Rubric — Scenario 2"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e8b3354b-5830-4547-91a0-f5b7d5e503e0","uuid":"dcbecf22-4899-4e77-8e77-84c5759c9367","timestamp":"2026-04-17T10:31:34.882Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\noss-to-wim\\aesthetic-services\\C01\\PA.md","content":"# PENILAIAN PRESTASI / PERFORMANCE ASSESSMENT\n\n**Kod / Code:** S960-002-3:2020-C01/PA\n**Competency Unit:** C01 — Body Consultation / *Konsultasi Badan*\n**Paper Colour / Warna Kertas:** LIGHT BLUE / BIRU MUDA\n**Duration / Tempoh:** 60 Minutes / 60 Minit (3 × 20 min scenarios)\n**Total Marks / Jumlah Markah:** 100\n**Passing Mark / Markah Lulus:** 70/100 (minimum Score 3/5 on ALL rubric criteria)\n\n---\n\n## Arahan / Instructions\n\n1. You will assess THREE (3) client consultation scenarios in sequence.\n2. Each scenario is 15–20 minutes and is assessed independently.\n3. For each scenario, score the candidate on FOUR (4) rubric criteria using a 5-point scale.\n4. A score of **3 or above** on each criterion is required to PASS that criterion.\n5. Any criterion scored **2 or below** = NOT YET COMPETENT for that scenario.\n6. Candidate must pass ALL criteria in at least 2 of 3 scenarios to be declared COMPETENT.\n7. Record marks in the tables below. Provide written feedback where scoring ≤ 2.\n\n---\n\n## SENARIO 1 — Saringan Sejarah Kesihatan / Health History Screening\n\n**Client Profile:** Madam Rosnah, 42 years old, female office manager. Presents with persistent fatigue\nand mild lower-back ache. She has hypertension (on medication) and a known shellfish allergy.\nShe has never received body therapy services before.\n\n**Task:** Conduct a full body consultation from work area preparation through contraindication screening,\nBMI calculation, and post-consultation advice. Duration: 15–20 minutes.\n\n**NOSS Reference:** WA 1 (1.1–1.3), WA 2 (2.1–2.3), WA 3 (3.1–3.2, 3.6–3.7, 3.9–3.11), WA 4 (4.1–4.4)\n\n### Rubrik Penilaian — Senario 1 / Assessment Rubric — Scenario 1\n\n| Kriteria / Criteria | 5 — Cemerlang | 4 — Memuaskan | 3 — Kompeten | 2 — Sedang Membangun | 1 — Tidak Kompeten | Markah |\n|---------------------|---------------|----------------|--------------|----------------------|--------------------|--------|\n| **S1-A Communication Effectiveness** (*Keberkesanan Komunikasi*) | Greets professionally; explains all steps clearly; uses empathetic, positive language; checks client understanding throughout; bilingual where appropriate | Greets and explains most steps; mostly clear communication; minor lapses in rapport | Adequate greeting and explanation; client understood key steps; basic professional conduct maintained | Communication partial; some steps not explained; client visibly confused at least once | No professional greeting; steps unexplained; client confused or uncomfortable throughout | /5 |\n| **S1-B Health & Allergy Data Collection** (*Pengumpulan Data Kesihatan & Alahan*) | ALL fields in personal profile recorded; hypertension medication AND shellfish allergy both documented; PDPA consent obtained; contraindications checklist fully completed and verified | Hypertension and allergy recorded; PDPA obtained; 1–2 minor fields missed | Hypertension OR allergy recorded; PDPA obtained; consultation card mostly complete | One major contraindication missed (hypertension or allergy not recorded) | Both contraindications missed; PDPA not obtained | /5 |\n| **S1-C Skin Condition Assessment Accuracy** (*Ketepatan Penilaian Kulit*) | Body type, posture (3 views), figure faults, skin/muscular/adipose/cellulite all assessed and correctly classified with explanation | All assessments done; classification correct; minimal explanation given | Most assessments done; at least 4 of 6 body analysis components completed | Assessments incomplete; fewer than 4 body analysis components; significant inaccuracies | No structured body analysis performed | /5 |\n| **S1-D Recommendation Appropriateness** (*Kesesuaian Cadangan*) | Salon service plan avoids electrotherapy (contraindicated by hypertension); safe alternatives recommended; shellfish-derived products excluded; home care complete and appropriate | Service plan appropriate; safe alternatives offered; 1 minor oversight in exclusion | Electrotherapy contraindication acknowledged; safe treatment offered; home care provided | Service plan partially appropriate; one unsafe recommendation present | Contraindications ignored in service plan; potentially harmful treatment recommended | /5 |\n\n**Subtotal Scenario 1:** \\_\\_\\_\\_ / 20 &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; **Pass (≥12/20, no criterion <3):** ☐ YES &nbsp; ☐ NO\n\n---\n\n## SENARIO 2 — Analisis Kulit & Komposisi Badan / Skin & Body Composition Analysis\n\n**Client Profile:** Ms. Adilah, 28 years old, female, post-pregnancy (8 months postpartum). She is\nconcerned about stretch marks (*striae*) on her abdomen and thighs, loose skin, and excess adipose\naround the waist. No known allergies. Currently breastfeeding.\n\n**Task:** Perform detailed skin condition analysis, body composition assessment, BMI calculation,\nand design a safe service plan appropriate for postpartum and breastfeeding status.\nDuration: 15–20 minutes.\n\n**NOSS Reference:** WA 3 (3.3–3.8), WA 4 (4.1–4.2)\n\n### Rubrik Penilaian — Senario 2 / Assessment Rubric — Scenario 2","numLines":60,"startLine":1,"totalLines":153}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01UwG7r11P66bK5t31DotW4N","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a good understanding of the PA files. The aesthetic-services PA files use a 5-point scale rubric format, while tuinalogy uses a different format (point-based tables), and BEV uses yet another format (marks-based tasks).\n\nThe story asks me to:\n1. Create `_tools/rubric-standardizer.py` that validates all PA files use standard rubric format (competency dimension | level descriptor | score | evidence)\n2. CLI command `uv run pytest tests/test_rubric_standards.py -v` audits all PA*.md files against standard format and reports compliance %\n\n\n3. Generate a report showing compliance percentage and identify which rubrics need reformatting\n\nI'll need to build validation and reformatting functions, create a standard rubric template as reference, and set up the test suite to audit all PA files. Let me examine a few more PA files to get a complete picture of the formatting variations I'm working with.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2649,"cache_read_input_tokens":36838,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2649},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e8b3354b-5830-4547-91a0-f5b7d5e503e0","uuid":"87af6366-f767-4d51-9260-43aa0a895a71"}
