{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KMiRyiwpuuy9GGRqYcwsvY","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# PENILAIAN PRESTASI (Performance Assessment)\n2\t\n3\t**Kod:** IT-020-3:2013-C01/PA\n4\t**Kertas Warna:** BIRU MUDA (Light Blue / Ocean Blue)\n5\t\n6\t---\n7\t\n8\t| | |\n9\t|---|---|\n10\t| **Kod Program / Programme Code** | IT-020-3:2013 |\n11\t| **Nama Program / Programme Name** | Computer System Operation (Operasi Sistem Komputer) |\n12\t| **Tahap / Level** | 3 |\n13\t| **No. dan Tajuk Unit Kompetensi** | CoCu 1: Computer System Set-up (Persediaan Sistem Komputer) |\n14\t| **Tempoh / Duration** | 3 hours |\n15\t| **Jumlah Markah / Total Marks** | 100 |\n16\t| **Markah Lulus / Pass Mark** | As per institutional and JPK requirements |\n17\t\n18\t---\n19\t\n20\t## Arahan kepada Pelatih / Instructions to Trainee\n21\t\n22\t1. This is a PRACTICAL examination. You will be assessed on your ability to perform a complete computer system set-up.\n23\t2. You will be given a job request and a set of hardware and software. You must complete the full set-up cycle.\n24\t3. You will be assessed on: **Process** (how you do it), **Output** (the result), **Attitude** (professionalism), **Safety** (ESD and electrical), and **Environmental** compliance.\n25\t4. You must wear an anti-static wrist strap throughout the hardware assembly phase.\n26\t5. All work must be documented on the provided set-up report form.\n27\t\n28\t---\n29\t\n30\t## Arahan kepada Penilai / Instructions to Assessor\n31\t\n32\t- Provide each trainee with a workstation, hardware components, tools, and a simulated job request.\n33\t- Observe each trainee continuously during the assessment.\n34\t- Do NOT assist the trainee unless there is a safety hazard.\n35\t- Mark each criterion on the assessment rubric as the trainee works.\n36\t- Verify the final output (working system, completed report) at the end.\n37\t\n38\t---\n39\t\n40\t## Tugasan / Task Description\n41\t\n42\t**Scenario:** You are a Level 3 Computer System Technician. You receive the following job request:\n43\t\n44\t| Field | Details |\n45\t|-------|---------|\n46\t| Job request number | PA-2026-001 |\n47\t| Requested by | Human Resources Department |\n48\t| Priority | Normal |\n49\t| Description | Set up a new desktop PC for a new employee |\n50\t| CPU | Intel Core i5 (LGA1700) |"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e8b3354b-5830-4547-91a0-f5b7d5e503e0","uuid":"c2e4d4dd-ebf2-4a05-8d99-0b64c06d944f","timestamp":"2026-04-17T10:31:43.628Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\noss-to-wim\\it-computer-system\\L3-C01\\PA.md","content":"# PENILAIAN PRESTASI (Performance Assessment)\n\n**Kod:** IT-020-3:2013-C01/PA\n**Kertas Warna:** BIRU MUDA (Light Blue / Ocean Blue)\n\n---\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| **Kod Program / Programme Code** | IT-020-3:2013 |\n| **Nama Program / Programme Name** | Computer System Operation (Operasi Sistem Komputer) |\n| **Tahap / Level** | 3 |\n| **No. dan Tajuk Unit Kompetensi** | CoCu 1: Computer System Set-up (Persediaan Sistem Komputer) |\n| **Tempoh / Duration** | 3 hours |\n| **Jumlah Markah / Total Marks** | 100 |\n| **Markah Lulus / Pass Mark** | As per institutional and JPK requirements |\n\n---\n\n## Arahan kepada Pelatih / Instructions to Trainee\n\n1. This is a PRACTICAL examination. You will be assessed on your ability to perform a complete computer system set-up.\n2. You will be given a job request and a set of hardware and software. You must complete the full set-up cycle.\n3. You will be assessed on: **Process** (how you do it), **Output** (the result), **Attitude** (professionalism), **Safety** (ESD and electrical), and **Environmental** compliance.\n4. You must wear an anti-static wrist strap throughout the hardware assembly phase.\n5. All work must be documented on the provided set-up report form.\n\n---\n\n## Arahan kepada Penilai / Instructions to Assessor\n\n- Provide each trainee with a workstation, hardware components, tools, and a simulated job request.\n- Observe each trainee continuously during the assessment.\n- Do NOT assist the trainee unless there is a safety hazard.\n- Mark each criterion on the assessment rubric as the trainee works.\n- Verify the final output (working system, completed report) at the end.\n\n---\n\n## Tugasan / Task Description\n\n**Scenario:** You are a Level 3 Computer System Technician. You receive the following job request:\n\n| Field | Details |\n|-------|---------|\n| Job request number | PA-2026-001 |\n| Requested by | Human Resources Department |\n| Priority | Normal |\n| Description | Set up a new desktop PC for a new employee |\n| CPU | Intel Core i5 (LGA1700) |","numLines":50,"startLine":1,"totalLines":170}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01RMwJtRxrzvG1hbjmJPXii5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have a good picture of the PA file formats across subjects. Let me now plan the implementation.\n\n## Current State\nPA files exist across 4 subjects (21 total). They have very different formats:\n- Aesthetic: 5-point scale rubrics with `Criteria | 5-desc | 4-desc | 3-desc | 2-desc | 1-desc | Score` columns\n- BEV: Task-based with marks allocation, no structured rubric columns  \n- Tuinalogy: Point-based tables with `评分项 | 满分 | 评分` \n- IT: Mixed format\n\n## Problem Identified\nNeed to: (1) define a standard rubric format, (2) create a validator tool, (3) create tests that audit compliance.\n\n## Planned Changes\n- Create `_reference/standard-rubric-template.md` - defines the standard format\n- Create `_tools/rubric-standardizer.py` - `validate_rubric_format()` + `reformat_rubric()` functions\n- Create `tests/test_rubric_standards.py` - pytest tests including `test_pa_rubric_format`\n\n<plan>\n{\n  \"files_to_create\": [\"_reference/standard-rubric-template.md\", \"_tools/rubric-standardizer.py\", \"tests/test_rubric_standards.py\"],\n  \"files_to_modify\": [],\n  \"functions_to_add\": [\"validate_rubric_format\", \"reformat_rubric\", \"generate_compliance_report\", \"test_pa_rubric_format\"],\n  \"estimated_loc\": 210\n}\n</plan>\n\nLet me check what's already in `_reference/` and the existing test patterns:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1099,"cache_read_input_tokens":39487,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1099},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e8b3354b-5830-4547-91a0-f5b7d5e503e0","uuid":"42114341-7aa0-4029-95ce-8fb399a581eb"}
