{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01ERcvY3Z6fjvKKMZAkbPKX7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QjPi8XnEMJagvFLRRmFUQk","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\noss-to-wim\\_reference\\standard-rubric-template.md","content":"# Standard Rubric Template — WIM Performance Assessment (PA)\n\n## Purpose\n\nDefines the mandatory format for all PA rubric tables across all NOSS WIM subjects\n(Tuinalogy, BEV, Aesthetic, IT). Every PA file must contain at least one compliant\nrubric table for the validator to report it as compliant.\n\n## Standard Rubric Format\n\nEach rubric table MUST have the four required column headers (in any order, case-insensitive):\n\n| Competency Dimension | Level Descriptor | Score | Evidence |\n|----------------------|------------------|-------|----------|\n| (criterion name)     | (what the level means) | (numeric) | (observable proof) |\n\n### Column definitions\n\n| Column | Aliases accepted | Description |\n|--------|-----------------|-------------|\n| **Competency Dimension** | Criteria, 评分项, Kriteria, Dimension | The skill or behaviour being assessed |\n| **Level Descriptor** | Descriptor, Description, 满分, Level, Standard | Describes what competent performance looks like |\n| **Score** | Marks, 评分, Markah, Points, Max | Numeric score or maximum points allocated |\n| **Evidence** | Evidence Required, Proof, Observable, 证据 | Observable proof that criterion was met |\n\n## Minimum Requirements\n\n1. Every PA file must contain at least one rubric table\n2. Rubric tables must have ≥ 3 columns matching the four required headers\n3. A rubric table must have at least 2 data rows (beyond the header row)\n4. Total marks must be traceable (either per-criterion or via a summary table)\n\n## Passing Score Convention\n\n- Competency-based: Minimum 70% (JPK standard) or as specified in the CU\n- Criterion-based: Minimum Score 3/5 on descriptive rubrics (5-point scale)\n- Point-based: ≥ 70/100 unless the NOSS CoCU specifies otherwise\n\n## Paper Colour Reference\n\n| Document Code | Paper Colour |\n|---------------|-------------|\n| PA | Light Blue / Biru Muda |\n| KA | Pink / Merah Jambu |\n| KP | White / Putih |\n| KT | Pink / Merah Jambu |\n| KK | Blue / Biru |\n| PM-teori | Yellow / Kuning |\n| PM-amali | Yellow / Kuning |\n\n## Example — Compliant Rubric Table\n\n| Competency Dimension | Level Descriptor | Score | Evidence |\n|----------------------|------------------|-------|----------|\n| Client Communication | Greets professionally; explains all steps; empathetic language | 5 | Verbal response; client body language |\n| Safety Procedure | All PPE donned correctly before entering work area | 10 | Direct observation checklist |\n\n## Example — Non-Compliant Table (missing Evidence column)\n\n| Criteria | Description | Marks |\n|----------|-------------|-------|\n| Communication | Good verbal skills | 5 |\n\n*Fix: add an Evidence column.*\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":772,"cache_read_input_tokens":41501,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":772},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e8b3354b-5830-4547-91a0-f5b7d5e503e0","uuid":"cc6ce797-dd05-4dde-8522-135f9fd4c572"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QjPi8XnEMJagvFLRRmFUQk","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\noss-to-wim\\_reference\\standard-rubric-template.md"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e8b3354b-5830-4547-91a0-f5b7d5e503e0","uuid":"89e82a80-133e-44cf-90b3-8ca3df1ec3a9","timestamp":"2026-04-17T10:32:18.306Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"create","filePath":"C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\noss-to-wim\\_reference\\standard-rubric-template.md","content":"# Standard Rubric Template — WIM Performance Assessment (PA)\n\n## Purpose\n\nDefines the mandatory format for all PA rubric tables across all NOSS WIM subjects\n(Tuinalogy, BEV, Aesthetic, IT). Every PA file must contain at least one compliant\nrubric table for the validator to report it as compliant.\n\n## Standard Rubric Format\n\nEach rubric table MUST have the four required column headers (in any order, case-insensitive):\n\n| Competency Dimension | Level Descriptor | Score | Evidence |\n|----------------------|------------------|-------|----------|\n| (criterion name)     | (what the level means) | (numeric) | (observable proof) |\n\n### Column definitions\n\n| Column | Aliases accepted | Description |\n|--------|-----------------|-------------|\n| **Competency Dimension** | Criteria, 评分项, Kriteria, Dimension | The skill or behaviour being assessed |\n| **Level Descriptor** | Descriptor, Description, 满分, Level, Standard | Describes what competent performance looks like |\n| **Score** | Marks, 评分, Markah, Points, Max | Numeric score or maximum points allocated |\n| **Evidence** | Evidence Required, Proof, Observable, 证据 | Observable proof that criterion was met |\n\n## Minimum Requirements\n\n1. Every PA file must contain at least one rubric table\n2. Rubric tables must have ≥ 3 columns matching the four required headers\n3. A rubric table must have at least 2 data rows (beyond the header row)\n4. Total marks must be traceable (either per-criterion or via a summary table)\n\n## Passing Score Convention\n\n- Competency-based: Minimum 70% (JPK standard) or as specified in the CU\n- Criterion-based: Minimum Score 3/5 on descriptive rubrics (5-point scale)\n- Point-based: ≥ 70/100 unless the NOSS CoCU specifies otherwise\n\n## Paper Colour Reference\n\n| Document Code | Paper Colour |\n|---------------|-------------|\n| PA | Light Blue / Biru Muda |\n| KA | Pink / Merah Jambu |\n| KP | White / Putih |\n| KT | Pink / Merah Jambu |\n| KK | Blue / Biru |\n| PM-teori | Yellow / Kuning |\n| PM-amali | Yellow / Kuning |\n\n## Example — Compliant Rubric Table\n\n| Competency Dimension | Level Descriptor | Score | Evidence |\n|----------------------|------------------|-------|----------|\n| Client Communication | Greets professionally; explains all steps; empathetic language | 5 | Verbal response; client body language |\n| Safety Procedure | All PPE donned correctly before entering work area | 10 | Direct observation checklist |\n\n## Example — Non-Compliant Table (missing Evidence column)\n\n| Criteria | Description | Marks |\n|----------|-------------|-------|\n| Communication | Good verbal skills | 5 |\n\n*Fix: add an Evidence column.*\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01D96t1YPrrUnmHvPxgXJJZx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013Z71NcDPZausf6HgAJdxEH","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\noss-to-wim\\_tools\\rubric-standardizer.py","content":"\"\"\"rubric-standardizer.py — Validate and reformat PA rubric tables (US-041).\n\nUsage:\n    uv run python _tools/rubric-standardizer.py [--report]\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport re\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent\n\n# Column header aliases mapped to canonical names\n_ALIASES: dict[str, str] = {\n    # Competency Dimension\n    \"competency dimension\": \"dimension\",\n    \"criteria\": \"dimension\",\n    \"评分项\": \"dimension\",\n    \"kriteria\": \"dimension\",\n    \"dimension\": \"dimension\",\n    \"criterion\": \"dimension\",\n    # Level Descriptor\n    \"level descriptor\": \"descriptor\",\n    \"descriptor\": \"descriptor\",\n    \"description\": \"descriptor\",\n    \"满分\": \"descriptor\",\n    \"standard\": \"descriptor\",\n    \"level\": \"descriptor\",\n    # Score\n    \"score\": \"score\",\n    \"marks\": \"score\",\n    \"评分\": \"score\",\n    \"markah\": \"score\",\n    \"points\": \"score\",\n    \"max\": \"score\",\n    # Evidence\n    \"evidence\": \"evidence\",\n    \"evidence required\": \"evidence\",\n    \"observable\": \"evidence\",\n    \"proof\": \"evidence\",\n    \"证据\": \"evidence\",\n}\n\n_REQUIRED = {\"dimension\", \"descriptor\", \"score\", \"evidence\"}\n\n\ndef _parse_table_headers(header_row: str) -> list[str]:\n    \"\"\"Return canonical column names from a markdown table header row.\"\"\"\n    cells = [c.strip().lower() for c in header_row.strip().strip(\"|\").split(\"|\")]\n    return [_ALIASES.get(c, c) for c in cells if c]\n\n\ndef _table_blocks(text: str) -> list[list[str]]:\n    \"\"\"Extract all markdown table blocks (list of row strings) from text.\"\"\"\n    tables: list[list[str]] = []\n    current: list[str] = []\n    for line in text.splitlines():\n        if re.match(r\"^\\s*\\|\", line):\n            current.append(line)\n        else:\n            if len(current) >= 2:\n                tables.append(current)\n            current = []\n    if len(current) >= 2:\n        tables.append(current)\n    return tables\n\n\ndef _is_separator(row: str) -> bool:\n    return bool(re.match(r\"^\\s*\\|[\\s|:-]+\\|\\s*$\", row))\n\n\ndef _data_rows(block: list[str]) -> list[str]:\n    \"\"\"Return data rows (skip header + separator rows).\"\"\"\n    rows = [r for r in block if not _is_separator(r)]\n    return rows[1:] if rows else []\n\n\ndef validate_rubric_format(path: Path) -> dict[str, object]:\n    \"\"\"Validate a PA file against the standard rubric format.\n\n    Returns a dict with keys:\n        file (str), compliant (bool), issues (list[str]),\n        rubric_table_count (int), compliant_tables (int)\n    \"\"\"\n    text = path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    tables = _table_blocks(text)\n\n    if not tables:\n        return {\n            \"file\": str(path.relative_to(ROOT)),\n            \"compliant\": False,\n            \"issues\": [\"No markdown table found in PA file\"],\n            \"rubric_table_count\": 0,\n            \"compliant_tables\": 0,\n        }\n\n    issues: list[str] = []\n    compliant_count = 0\n\n    for i, block in enumerate(tables, 1):\n        if not block:\n            continue\n        headers = _parse_table_headers(block[0])\n        canonical = set(headers)\n        missing = _REQUIRED - canonical\n        data = _data_rows(block)\n\n        if missing:\n            issues.append(f\"Table {i}: missing columns {sorted(missing)}\")\n            continue\n        if len(data) < 2:\n            issues.append(f\"Table {i}: fewer than 2 data rows ({len(data)} found)\")\n            continue\n        compliant_count += 1\n\n    return {\n        \"file\": str(path.relative_to(ROOT)),\n        \"compliant\": compliant_count > 0,\n        \"issues\": issues,\n        \"rubric_table_count\": len(tables),\n        \"compliant_tables\": compliant_count,\n    }\n\n\ndef reformat_rubric(path: Path) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Return file text with a standard-format rubric appended if none exists.\n\n    Only adds a placeholder rubric; does not modify existing content.\n    \"\"\"\n    result = validate_rubric_format(path)\n    if result[\"compliant\"]:\n        return path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n\n    placeholder = (\n        \"\\n\\n---\\n\\n\"\n        \"## Standard Rubric (Auto-generated placeholder — please fill in)\\n\\n\"\n        \"| Competency Dimension | Level Descriptor | Score | Evidence |\\n\"\n        \"|----------------------|------------------|-------|----------|\\n\"\n        \"| *(criterion 1)* | *(description of competent performance)* | 0 | *(observable proof)* |\\n\"\n        \"| *(criterion 2)* | *(description of competent performance)* | 0 | *(observable proof)* |\\n\"\n    )\n    return path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\") + placeholder\n\n\ndef generate_compliance_report(root: Path = ROOT) -> dict[str, object]:\n    \"\"\"Scan all PA*.md files and return a compliance report.\"\"\"\n    pa_files = sorted(root.glob(\"**/PA*.md\"))\n    results = [validate_rubric_format(p) for p in pa_files]\n\n    total = len(results)\n    compliant = sum(1 for r in results if r[\"compliant\"])\n    pct = round(100 * compliant / total, 1) if total else 0.0\n\n    non_compliant = [r for r in results if not r[\"compliant\"]]\n\n    return {\n        \"total_files\": total,\n        \"compliant_files\": compliant,\n        \"compliance_pct\": pct,\n        \"non_compliant\": non_compliant,\n        \"all_results\": results,\n    }\n\n\ndef _print_report(report: dict[str, object]) -> None:\n    print(f\"\\n=== PA Rubric Compliance Report ===\")\n    print(f\"Files scanned : {report['total_files']}\")\n    print(f\"Compliant     : {report['compliant_files']}\")\n    print(f\"Compliance %  : {report['compliance_pct']}%\")\n\n    non_compliant = report[\"non_compliant\"]  # type: ignore[index]\n    if non_compliant:\n        print(f\"\\nNon-compliant files ({len(non_compliant)}):\")\n        for r in non_compliant:\n            print(f\"  {r['file']}\")\n            for issue in r[\"issues\"]:  # type: ignore[union-attr]\n                print(f\"    - {issue}\")\n    else:\n        print(\"\\nAll PA files are compliant.\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    report = generate_compliance_report()\n    _print_report(report)\n    sys.exit(0 if report[\"compliance_pct\"] == 100.0 else 1)\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":893,"cache_read_input_tokens":42273,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":893},"output_tokens":59,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e8b3354b-5830-4547-91a0-f5b7d5e503e0","uuid":"f1b887d4-d1e0-4668-9f8e-fcbab4e9ec04"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013Z71NcDPZausf6HgAJdxEH","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\noss-to-wim\\_tools\\rubric-standardizer.py"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e8b3354b-5830-4547-91a0-f5b7d5e503e0","uuid":"3ee14363-b18e-46bb-863e-f9241f204bb8","timestamp":"2026-04-17T10:32:41.257Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"create","filePath":"C:\\Users\\Jyue\\Documents\\1-projects\\noss-to-wim\\_tools\\rubric-standardizer.py","content":"\"\"\"rubric-standardizer.py — Validate and reformat PA rubric tables (US-041).\n\nUsage:\n    uv run python _tools/rubric-standardizer.py [--report]\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport re\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent\n\n# Column header aliases mapped to canonical names\n_ALIASES: dict[str, str] = {\n    # Competency Dimension\n    \"competency dimension\": \"dimension\",\n    \"criteria\": \"dimension\",\n    \"评分项\": \"dimension\",\n    \"kriteria\": \"dimension\",\n    \"dimension\": \"dimension\",\n    \"criterion\": \"dimension\",\n    # Level Descriptor\n    \"level descriptor\": \"descriptor\",\n    \"descriptor\": \"descriptor\",\n    \"description\": \"descriptor\",\n    \"满分\": \"descriptor\",\n    \"standard\": \"descriptor\",\n    \"level\": \"descriptor\",\n    # Score\n    \"score\": \"score\",\n    \"marks\": \"score\",\n    \"评分\": \"score\",\n    \"markah\": \"score\",\n    \"points\": \"score\",\n    \"max\": \"score\",\n    # Evidence\n    \"evidence\": \"evidence\",\n    \"evidence required\": \"evidence\",\n    \"observable\": \"evidence\",\n    \"proof\": \"evidence\",\n    \"证据\": \"evidence\",\n}\n\n_REQUIRED = {\"dimension\", \"descriptor\", \"score\", \"evidence\"}\n\n\ndef _parse_table_headers(header_row: str) -> list[str]:\n    \"\"\"Return canonical column names from a markdown table header row.\"\"\"\n    cells = [c.strip().lower() for c in header_row.strip().strip(\"|\").split(\"|\")]\n    return [_ALIASES.get(c, c) for c in cells if c]\n\n\ndef _table_blocks(text: str) -> list[list[str]]:\n    \"\"\"Extract all markdown table blocks (list of row strings) from text.\"\"\"\n    tables: list[list[str]] = []\n    current: list[str] = []\n    for line in text.splitlines():\n        if re.match(r\"^\\s*\\|\", line):\n            current.append(line)\n        else:\n            if len(current) >= 2:\n                tables.append(current)\n            current = []\n    if len(current) >= 2:\n        tables.append(current)\n    return tables\n\n\ndef _is_separator(row: str) -> bool:\n    return bool(re.match(r\"^\\s*\\|[\\s|:-]+\\|\\s*$\", row))\n\n\ndef _data_rows(block: list[str]) -> list[str]:\n    \"\"\"Return data rows (skip header + separator rows).\"\"\"\n    rows = [r for r in block if not _is_separator(r)]\n    return rows[1:] if rows else []\n\n\ndef validate_rubric_format(path: Path) -> dict[str, object]:\n    \"\"\"Validate a PA file against the standard rubric format.\n\n    Returns a dict with keys:\n        file (str), compliant (bool), issues (list[str]),\n        rubric_table_count (int), compliant_tables (int)\n    \"\"\"\n    text = path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    tables = _table_blocks(text)\n\n    if not tables:\n        return {\n            \"file\": str(path.relative_to(ROOT)),\n            \"compliant\": False,\n            \"issues\": [\"No markdown table found in PA file\"],\n            \"rubric_table_count\": 0,\n            \"compliant_tables\": 0,\n        }\n\n    issues: list[str] = []\n    compliant_count = 0\n\n    for i, block in enumerate(tables, 1):\n        if not block:\n            continue\n        headers = _parse_table_headers(block[0])\n        canonical = set(headers)\n        missing = _REQUIRED - canonical\n        data = _data_rows(block)\n\n        if missing:\n            issues.append(f\"Table {i}: missing columns {sorted(missing)}\")\n            continue\n        if len(data) < 2:\n            issues.append(f\"Table {i}: fewer than 2 data rows ({len(data)} found)\")\n            continue\n        compliant_count += 1\n\n    return {\n        \"file\": str(path.relative_to(ROOT)),\n        \"compliant\": compliant_count > 0,\n        \"issues\": issues,\n        \"rubric_table_count\": len(tables),\n        \"compliant_tables\": compliant_count,\n    }\n\n\ndef reformat_rubric(path: Path) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Return file text with a standard-format rubric appended if none exists.\n\n    Only adds a placeholder rubric; does not modify existing content.\n    \"\"\"\n    result = validate_rubric_format(path)\n    if result[\"compliant\"]:\n        return path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\n\n    placeholder = (\n        \"\\n\\n---\\n\\n\"\n        \"## Standard Rubric (Auto-generated placeholder — please fill in)\\n\\n\"\n        \"| Competency Dimension | Level Descriptor | Score | Evidence |\\n\"\n        \"|----------------------|------------------|-------|----------|\\n\"\n        \"| *(criterion 1)* | *(description of competent performance)* | 0 | *(observable proof)* |\\n\"\n        \"| *(criterion 2)* | *(description of competent performance)* | 0 | *(observable proof)* |\\n\"\n    )\n    return path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\") + placeholder\n\n\ndef generate_compliance_report(root: Path = ROOT) -> dict[str, object]:\n    \"\"\"Scan all PA*.md files and return a compliance report.\"\"\"\n    pa_files = sorted(root.glob(\"**/PA*.md\"))\n    results = [validate_rubric_format(p) for p in pa_files]\n\n    total = len(results)\n    compliant = sum(1 for r in results if r[\"compliant\"])\n    pct = round(100 * compliant / total, 1) if total else 0.0\n\n    non_compliant = [r for r in results if not r[\"compliant\"]]\n\n    return {\n        \"total_files\": total,\n        \"compliant_files\": compliant,\n        \"compliance_pct\": pct,\n        \"non_compliant\": non_compliant,\n        \"all_results\": results,\n    }\n\n\ndef _print_report(report: dict[str, object]) -> None:\n    print(f\"\\n=== PA Rubric Compliance Report ===\")\n    print(f\"Files scanned : {report['total_files']}\")\n    print(f\"Compliant     : {report['compliant_files']}\")\n    print(f\"Compliance %  : {report['compliance_pct']}%\")\n\n    non_compliant = report[\"non_compliant\"]  # type: ignore[index]\n    if non_compliant:\n        print(f\"\\nNon-compliant files ({len(non_compliant)}):\")\n        for r in non_compliant:\n            print(f\"  {r['file']}\")\n            for issue in r[\"issues\"]:  # type: ignore[union-attr]\n                print(f\"    - {issue}\")\n    else:\n        print(\"\\nAll PA files are compliant.\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    report = generate_compliance_report()\n    _print_report(report)\n    sys.exit(0 if report[\"compliance_pct\"] == 100.0 else 1)\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null}}
